 "notes": {
  "attempt1": "the plan's rules 1-3 as written (leg max 0.5, 2 smoothing passes). Its blend and exports were overwritten by variation1 in SourceArt/Warden/V5_5w; its numbers (reweight stats, after_attempt1 measurement) are kept here.",
  "variation1": "leg max 0.35, 3 smoothing passes; everything else as the plan. This is what SourceArt/Warden/V5_5w holds. Both attempts fail the metric.",
  "pass": "pass = largest ratio <= 1.8 and the worst single frame has < 0.5 % of wool edges above 1.5; pass_strict_union uses the share of edges above 1.5 in ANY frame.",
  "diagnosis": {
   "unmodified_shoulder_and_chest_wool": "~2,190 of the ~11,000 bad edges after the reweight are between vertices that no rule touches (z 1.6 to 2.5, |x| < 0.25: clavicle/upperarm/spine splits); this alone is 4.3 % of wool edges.",
   "foot_pinned_hem": "108 wool vertices at z 0.15-0.22 are weighted 100 % to the leg/foot bones in the master; they, and leather hem vertices weighted partly to robe bones, cause every wool edge above 5x at z < 0.4 (158 wool edges, 168 leather edges, max 168x). The floor slabs on the sheets are these.",
   "leg_split_gradient": "f = 0.5 + x/0.6 changes the left/right leg share by about 1.7 % per cm; with the legs 1.2 m apart in the stride a 1 cm hem edge stretches about 1 + L * 2, so even L = 0.35 gives many edges at 1.5-3x.",
   "sleeve_flaps": "sleeve flap vertices that were weighted 98 % to robe bones (1,342 near-only vertices) now follow the forearm rigidly: good in walk, run and attack, but in TurnLeft90/TurnRight90 and ZombieAttack 25 % they fold into boxes at hip height."
  },
  "round3_try1": "V5_5w2 round 3 as specified: (A) wool+leather z<0.30 with >50% foot/ball take their 4 nearest robe vertices' weights + rule 2 blend, then 2 smoothing passes over z<0.4; (B) 626 flap vertices (z<1.57, formerly robe-weighted sleeve) back to master robe weights + rule 2 blend, 30% to spine_03 (z>1.2) or pelvis; (C) wool within 10 cm of a seam (changed vertex, L1 weight difference > 0.3) smoothed, 60 passes at LOD0 (scaled by edge length for LOD1/2). Base: leg max 0.35, 3 passes. Left thin floor spikes: 90 % of the remaining >5x low edges were leather vertices with exactly 0.5 foot + 0.5 calf, which '> 50 %' missed.\n",
  "round3_variation": "what SourceArt/Warden/V5_5w2 holds: as try 1 but the foot rule is 'thigh/calf/foot/ball share >= 0.30' (--pin-leg 0.3). Shorter floor spikes, same numbers elsewhere.",
  "metrics_caveat": "round 3 is judged by eye; the metric numbers are reported, not gated. The feather also smooths unchanged vertices near a seam, so changed_vertices is about 15.5k on LOD0."
 },
